# M3-22: the SERVER process was restarted (new ServerHello session GUID, same data dir: the session and its checkpoints persist) and the authority's game restarted
# too. The authority is sent the session's newest checkpoint (the start-save path of M3-21), loads it, and the avatars that checkpoint's manifest listed (the
# two of the "Save now" checkpoint of avatars.hostsim) are KEPT: the loaded save decides, not the session id. Nothing is dropped, nothing is spawned.
# Run by avatars_run.ps1 (vars: tcp, apw).
init
set game_time 6000
world sector add 100003
frame 60Hz 10
lua-raw x4mp.ui_ready {"v":1,"startmenu":true}
lua-raw x4mp.join {"v":1,"address":"127.0.0.1:${tcp}","name":"HostAlice","password":"","admin_password":"${apw}","role":"authority","team":"auto"}
frame 60Hz 360
expect-file extension/logs/x4mp.log avatars: 2 avatar record(s) restored
expect-file extension/logs/x4mp.log SessionSaveInfo:
expect-lua x4mp.load_save 3000 contains x4mp_
reload
frame 60Hz 240
expect-file extension/logs/x4mp.log resuming the session after an extension reload
load_save x4mp_restart_load
frame 60Hz 240
expect-file extension/logs/x4mp.log NodeReady sent
expect-file extension/logs/x4mp.log 2 of 2 avatar record(s) kept
expect-no-log avatar record(s) dropped
expect-no-log avatars: spawned the avatar of player
lua-raw x4mp.disconnect {"v":1}
frame 60Hz 30
expect-no-secret ${apw}
shutdown
